# Continuous Bovaro execution

Analysis, planning, documentation and project-memory updates are checkpoints,
not final deliverables.

After completing and verifying a phase:

1. Update the project memory.
2. Mark completed acceptance criteria.
3. Identify the next incomplete criterion.
4. Continue directly with the next implementation phase.
5. Do not wait for a new user message.

Do not stop after repository analysis, blocker identification, project-memory
installation, architecture documentation, branch/commit/PR creation or a phase
report. Complete all local code, tests, adapters, migrations and documentation
even when external credentials are unavailable.

